AUTHORS — Rudroid

Maintainer and first-party implementation
----------------------------------------
jenny92-tech <jennyliu90223@gmail.com>
  https://github.com/jenny92-tech/Rudroid
  Rust implementation, compatibility/runtime integration, native glue,
  title adaptations, resource tools and handheld validation.

Acknowledgements — reference framework
--------------------------------------
binarycounter and the Bogodroid contributors.
  C++ framework used as a behavioral reference and predecessor:
  https://github.com/binarycounter/Bogodroid

JohnnyOnFlame <https://github.com/JohnnyonFlame>
  Author of gmloader-net, a predecessor of the Bogodroid framework.

ChristopherHX <https://github.com/ChristopherHX>
  Author of libjnivm (MIT), the C++ reference JNI implementation.
  Rudroid's Rust JNI runtime is in crates/capability/android/jni_vm.

Third-party material
--------------------
The Android Open Source Project provides the BSD-2-Clause ARM64 jump-buffer
assembly and the Apache-2.0 JNI test fixture header. Their notices are retained.
Rust dependencies and optional native components keep their individual licenses;
see the root NOTICE, THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES and the optional vulkan-wsi/ bundle.
There are no libjnivm or tomlplusplus submodules in Rudroid.

First-party work uses the root noncommercial source-sharing LICENSE.
This list acknowledges references without claiming their authors wrote Rudroid's
Rust implementation. Earlier GPL copies retain their existing permissions.
